body:
When `sp.rootModulePaths` has more than one entry (e.g. a monorepo with nested modules, or a `go.work` build), this loop pushes the same `rule.InstRule` into `globRules` once per root:

```go
for _, root := range sp.rootModulePaths {
    globRules = append(globRules, targetRule{target: root + "/**", rule: r})
}
```

If two resolved root paths overlap as glob prefixes (e.g. `example.com/app` and `example.com/app/plugin` as separate modules), a dependency under the nested module matches both expanded globs. `runMatch`'s glob loop has no dedup:

```go
for _, gr := range globRules {
    if !rule.MatchGlobTarget(gr.target, dep.ImportPath) {
        continue
    }
    ...
    matched = append(matched, gr.rule)
}
```

The same rule instance gets appended twice, so the dependency ends up matched/hooked twice. Worth deduping either at expansion time (skip a root path that's a sub-path of another already-collected root) or at match time (skip a rule already present in `matched` for this dependency).

