This takes the parsed go.mod module path with no `golang.org/x/mod/module.CheckPath` validation, unlike the normal path (a few lines up) where `go/packages` has already validated the module path's syntax before populating `pkg.Module.Path`. A go.mod with an invalid module path would likely fail earlier in the Go toolchain anyway — still, aligning the two code paths would remove the inconsistency.

